        <h2>2. The writing belongs to us</h2>
        <p>
            The in-world recipes, the narrator voices, the site copy and
            the design are ours (or used here with permission). You can
            share a link, quote a bit with credit, and print a recipe to
            cook from. You can't republish the content as your own or use
            it commercially without asking first.
        </p>

        <h2>3. No scraping, no AI training</h2>
        <p>
            Don't scrape, crawl, bulk-download, or feed this site's content
            into a dataset, a language model, or an &ldquo;answer
            engine.&rdquo; Automated extraction of the content is not
            permitted, and a User-Agent that hides what it is doesn't
            change that.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you want the content in bulk - for a model, a product,
            a research corpus, anything - that's fine, it's just not
            free. Send &pound;{{ fee_gbp }} to
            <a href="mailto:{{ contact_email }}">{{ contact_email }}</a>,
            tell us where to send it, and we'll hand over a clean licensed
            copy. One payment, one copy. It is genuinely less effort than
            scraping it, and it's allowed.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Accounts and your Grimoire</h2>
        <p>
            You're responsible for what happens under your login and for
            keeping your password to yourself. Anything you save to your
            Grimoire is yours; we just store it. We can suspend an account
            that's being used to abuse the site or other people.
        </p>

        <h2>5. No warranty</h2>
        <p>
            The site is provided as-is. The recipes are tested in good
            faith, but you cook at your own risk - check your own
            allergens, temperatures and timings. The &ldquo;mundane
            truth&rdquo; behind each ritual is our best honest account of
            the real recipe, not a guarantee. We're not liable for loss
            arising from use of the site, except where the law says we
            can't exclude that.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Changes</h2>
        <p>
            We may update these terms. The date at the top changes when we
            do. Continuing to use the site after that means you're fine
            with the new version.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Contact</h2>
        <p>
            Questions, permission requests, or the &pound;{{ fee_gbp }}
            licensing offer above:
            <a href="mailto:{{ contact_email }}">{{ contact_email }}</a>.
        </p>
    </article>
{% endblock %}
